WEBVTT

00:02.640 --> 00:05.940
<b>I would like to avoid
unnecessary battle, that I would.</b>

00:06.650 --> 00:10.900
<b>Can you step aside and let me know
where Kanryu and Miss Megumi are?</b>

00:12.190 --> 00:15.870
<b>You need to ask me the whereabouts
of those two with that sakabato.</b>

00:17.320 --> 00:20.120
<b>I will answer... with this.</b>

01:55.970 --> 01:59.970
<b>EPISODE 12:
OKASHIRA -
AOSHI SHINOMORI</b>

02:02.680 --> 02:04.390
<b>The length of that blade...</b>

02:05.140 --> 02:07.430
<b>You're trying to fight
with just one wakizashi?</b>

02:07.430 --> 02:08.310
<b>Don't mock us!</b>

02:08.690 --> 02:10.350
<b>Kids should stay back.</b>

02:10.480 --> 02:11.310
<b>Damn you!</b>

02:11.480 --> 02:13.270
<b>I wish the same, that I do.</b>

02:15.110 --> 02:16.610
<b>Oh, um...</b>

02:17.650 --> 02:20.280
<b>Damn it, each and every one of you.</b>

02:20.280 --> 02:23.530
<b>Listen up! You better not have
a hard time against one little wakizashi!</b>

02:24.160 --> 02:25.790
<b>Hurry up, and get this over with!</b>

02:28.460 --> 02:30.710
<b>If that really was a wakizashi,</b>

02:30.710 --> 02:33.040
<b>I wouldn't have a hard time,
that I wouldn't.</b>

02:33.540 --> 02:36.710
<b>You seem to know
of the characteristics of a kodachi.</b>

02:37.170 --> 02:38.380
<b>Kodachi?</b>

02:38.380 --> 02:42.680
<b>Simply put, a sword that is between
a katana and a wakizashi, that it is.</b>

02:43.350 --> 02:46.390
<b>As it is shorter than a katana,
it lacks in offensive power.</b>

02:46.390 --> 02:50.440
<b>But as it is light and very adaptable,
it has high defensive power.</b>

02:51.310 --> 02:54.980
<b>To be on the offensive against that
would be highly disadvantageous.</b>

02:56.360 --> 02:57.190
<b>I see.</b>

02:57.860 --> 02:59.780
<b>Then I shall be the one to attack.</b>

03:01.410 --> 03:02.320
<b>So quick!</b>

03:05.120 --> 03:05.990
<b>Kenshin!</b>

03:06.200 --> 03:08.410
<b><i>A kick? Can this man be...</i></b>

03:08.620 --> 03:09.710
<b><i>just like Han'nya...</i></b>

03:09.910 --> 03:10.920
<b><i>a kenpo master!</i></b>

03:22.260 --> 03:23.090
<b>I see.</b>

03:23.640 --> 03:26.010
<b>You lay out an impenetrable defense
with the kodachi,</b>

03:26.260 --> 03:29.680
<b>but attack with the same kenpo as Han'nya.
That's your style.</b>

03:29.980 --> 03:32.900
<b>I was the one
that taught kenpo to Han'nya.</b>

03:35.900 --> 03:37.610
<b>The speed and weight of a master's fist</b>

03:37.610 --> 03:39.650
<b>is greatly different
than that of an apprentice.</b>

03:41.150 --> 03:44.990
<b>Battosai,
I have nothing personal against you.</b>

03:44.990 --> 03:48.160
<b>But as the most powerful Imperialist,
I will have you die right here.</b>

03:49.870 --> 03:55.170
<b>It seems like you are not fighting
for Kanryu's sake, that it doesn't.</b>

03:55.670 --> 03:56.630
<b>Of course not.</b>

03:57.750 --> 04:01.340
<b>Is it for the Tokugawa Shogunate
that fell with the revolution?</b>

04:03.340 --> 04:05.970
<b>If you are an Imperialist,
you should know</b>

04:05.970 --> 04:10.270
<b>how Yoshinobu Tokugawa acted
in the Battle of Toba-Fushimi.</b>

04:11.930 --> 04:14.900
<b>As soon as Yoshinobu,
the final Shogun of Tokugawa,</b>

04:14.900 --> 04:17.480
<b>found out the Shogunate army was inferior,</b>

04:17.480 --> 04:21.240
<b>he and his top retainers
left Osaka Castle by themselves,</b>

04:21.240 --> 04:22.950
<b>returning to Edo by battleship.</b>

04:23.900 --> 04:26.780
<b>He abandoned over 10,000 soldiers</b>

04:26.780 --> 04:29.290
<b>risking their lives
fighting on the battlefield.</b>

04:30.490 --> 04:32.450
<b>After he fled back to Edo,</b>

04:32.450 --> 04:35.500
<b>he decided on absolute compliance
at Kanei Temple in Ueno.</b>

04:35.670 --> 04:38.380
<b>After talks between Kaishu Katsu,
who was given full authority,</b>

04:38.380 --> 04:41.050
<b>and Takamori Saigo,
the imperial Edo Castle</b>

04:41.050 --> 04:44.050
<b>ended up being surrendered
with no bloodshed.</b>

04:44.800 --> 04:49.220
<b>And the Oniwaban Group ended
the Bakumatsu Era without fighting.</b>

04:51.310 --> 04:53.890
<b>We don't care
about the coward Tokugawa anymore.</b>

04:54.730 --> 04:57.770
<b>Our only regret is the fact
that we could not fight.</b>

04:58.810 --> 05:01.530
<b>There are no ifs in the flow of history,</b>

05:01.530 --> 05:03.780
<b>but had we fought back then...</b>

05:04.650 --> 05:07.780
<b>the victory in the revolution
would have belonged to the Shogunate.</b>

05:12.370 --> 05:16.040
<b>We would create a huge fire in Edo,
and then we, the Oniwaban Group,</b>

05:16.040 --> 05:20.340
<b>would kill the Imperial officers
at the heart of the army in the chaos.</b>

05:21.130 --> 05:23.420
<b>After that,
what remains is an unorderly mob.</b>

05:23.920 --> 05:27.680
<b>The Shogunate Army, superior in numbers,
can crush them all...</b>

05:28.260 --> 05:29.600
<b>and that's the end.</b>

05:31.180 --> 05:33.390
<b>No way you'd be able to do that!</b>

05:33.680 --> 05:35.270
<b>We can.</b>

05:35.270 --> 05:37.690
<b>Shall we replicate the incident here?</b>

05:38.350 --> 05:39.650
<b>Right here in Tokyo?</b>

05:40.820 --> 05:42.110
<b><i>Damn this guy.</i></b>

05:42.900 --> 05:45.950
<b>But doing something like that
at this point is completely meaningless.</b>

05:46.570 --> 05:50.070
<b>What has meaning right now is proof.</b>

05:50.700 --> 05:54.160
<b>Proof that superiority
in the Bakumatsu Revolution</b>

05:54.580 --> 05:56.580
<b>was embodied by us, the Oniwaban Group.</b>

06:00.250 --> 06:01.210
<b>Back in those days...</b>

06:02.000 --> 06:04.630
<b>many threw themselves into battle...</b>

06:05.130 --> 06:07.760
<b>whether Revolutionary warrior
or Shogunate samurai.</b>

06:08.680 --> 06:09.840
<b>We antagonized each other.</b>

06:10.340 --> 06:14.470
<b>But neither was righteous,
and neither was mistaken.</b>

06:15.220 --> 06:17.980
<b>We were simply concerned
for the future of this country</b>

06:17.980 --> 06:21.480
<b>and risked our lives for the peace
and happiness of the people.</b>

06:22.730 --> 06:24.730
<b>But you have none of that!</b>

06:24.730 --> 06:27.610
<b>What you have,
calmly saying you would raze a town,</b>

06:27.780 --> 06:31.280
<b>is nothing more than bloody,
ice-cold competitiveness!</b>

06:31.910 --> 06:34.370
<b>Both as a Revolutionary warrior
and a rurouni...</b>

06:35.080 --> 06:37.500
<b>I cannot sit quietly
and let you get away with it!</b>

06:38.460 --> 06:39.790
<b>Say what you want.</b>

06:40.500 --> 06:43.670
<b>Even if you became serious about this,
you have no chance of winning.</b>

06:43.790 --> 06:44.630
<b>Come on.</b>

06:51.640 --> 06:54.470
<b>Going from Hiten Mitsurugi-ryu Ryuutsuisen</b>

06:54.470 --> 06:56.350
<b>straight into a battojutsu
without landing.</b>

06:56.850 --> 06:58.600
<b>That's quite an attack,</b>

06:58.600 --> 07:01.770
<b>but you can't break my kodachi
with anything of that level.</b>

07:03.900 --> 07:05.190
<b><i>Damn it!</i></b>

07:05.190 --> 07:10.240
<b><i>Aoshi is merely a hired hand,
and yet he makes a fool out of me!</i></b>

07:10.910 --> 07:12.450
<b><i>First Megumi, now him.</i></b>

07:12.450 --> 07:14.700
<b><i>Each and every one. Each and every one!</i></b>

07:14.950 --> 07:17.290
<b><i>But now I figured it out!</i></b>

07:17.290 --> 07:21.790
<b><i>That man, like Battosai, is the type
that I can't control with money.</i></b>

07:21.790 --> 07:25.000
<b><i>He's a dangerous man that can
turn into a foe at any point in time!</i></b>

07:25.710 --> 07:27.460
<b><i>Battosai and Aoshi...</i></b>

07:27.460 --> 07:30.170
<b><i>is there a way for me
to get rid of both of them?</i></b>

07:30.170 --> 07:33.720
<b><i>Think, Kanryu. Some way? Some way?</i></b>

07:33.720 --> 07:35.640
<b><i>Something, something,
something, something!</i></b>

07:36.680 --> 07:41.310
<b>Um, Mr. Kanryu, what should we do
about the test of you-know-what?</b>

07:41.310 --> 07:43.100
<b>That's it!</b>

07:48.110 --> 07:50.280
<b>No matter how many times you attack,
it's useless.</b>

07:50.740 --> 07:55.320
<b>When concentrating on defense, my kodachi
will even protect me from rifle bullets.</b>

07:56.660 --> 08:00.450
<b><i>Not even Kenshin can land one blow on him.</i></b>

08:00.960 --> 08:03.920
<b><i>That, and, no matter how much
of an advantage he gains,</i></b>

08:03.920 --> 08:05.960
<b><i>he doesn't show one smile.</i></b>

08:05.960 --> 08:08.090
<b><i>That's truly
an ice-cold competitiveness.</i></b>

08:08.550 --> 08:11.800
<b><i>Damn it. My knees feel so weak.</i></b>

08:11.880 --> 08:12.720
<b>Kenshin!</b>

08:13.090 --> 08:14.930
<b>It's all right, that it is.</b>

08:15.390 --> 08:18.890
<b>I'd feel very sorry for Miss Megumi
if something like this defeats me,</b>

08:18.890 --> 08:21.020
<b>and I'd be too ashamed
to see Miss Kaoru again.</b>

08:21.180 --> 08:23.810
<b>And who knows what Sano would say to me?</b>

08:23.810 --> 08:24.650
<b>Besides...</b>

08:25.190 --> 08:29.070
<b>I finally see a way
to get past that kodachi, that I do.</b>

08:29.360 --> 08:32.030
<b>I'd like to say that's a bluff...</b>

08:32.900 --> 08:35.450
<b>but you're not one
to say things of that nature.</b>

08:36.490 --> 08:37.830
<b>So I'll have you show me...</b>

08:38.370 --> 08:39.540
<b>this so-called way.</b>

08:41.500 --> 08:42.830
<b>Too slow!</b>

08:43.000 --> 08:45.290
<b>What? He's holding
the bottom of the blade.</b>

08:49.460 --> 08:52.590
<b>Aoshi, the secret of your power</b>

08:52.880 --> 08:56.050
<b>is completely controlling the reach
between you and your opponent.</b>

08:56.390 --> 08:57.510
<b>Reach.</b>

08:58.510 --> 08:59.470
<b><i>Listen up, Yahiko.</i></b>

08:59.970 --> 09:01.140
<b><i>"Reach" is the distance</i></b>

09:01.140 --> 09:05.190
<b><i>in which you can make an attack
on your opponent in one move.</i></b>

09:05.770 --> 09:11.360
<b><i>The key for combat between higher-ranked
masters is to fight inside your own reach.</i></b>

09:12.360 --> 09:16.660
<b>It's easy to think that I'm
at an advantage with a katana.</b>

09:17.160 --> 09:21.080
<b>You can't help but create a blind spot
at one's center with a long reach.</b>

09:21.740 --> 09:24.330
<b>And you attack right at that blind spot.</b>

09:24.710 --> 09:28.130
<b>Then I shall just switch over
to the same reach as a kodachi,</b>

09:28.130 --> 09:30.170
<b>and the blind spot
should naturally disappear.</b>

09:30.670 --> 09:31.710
<b>So I see.</b>

09:31.920 --> 09:33.800
<b>Simply gripping a Japanese sword,</b>

09:34.340 --> 09:37.180
<b>especially the bottom,
where it is most dull,</b>

09:37.180 --> 09:39.350
<b>won't dig the blade
all the way down to the bone.</b>

09:39.850 --> 09:42.180
<b>Lose a battle to win the war, huh?</b>

09:42.970 --> 09:46.270
<b>I have now seen the essence of a hitokiri.</b>

09:47.900 --> 09:53.150
<b>In return, I will take you down with
the essence of the Oniwaban Group leader.</b>

09:56.200 --> 09:57.200
<b><i>So slow?</i></b>

09:57.200 --> 09:58.740
<b><i>What is this slow speed?</i></b>

10:04.790 --> 10:05.870
<b><i>This is...</i></b>

10:06.410 --> 10:07.330
<b><i>a sword dance?</i></b>

10:08.040 --> 10:10.170
<b><i>This is different
from a ritualistic sword dance!</i></b>

10:14.130 --> 10:15.590
<b>Stop it.</b>

10:15.880 --> 10:17.170
<b>You are used to swordsmanship</b>

10:17.170 --> 10:19.430
<b>that clearly differentiates
stillness from motion.</b>

10:19.930 --> 10:23.470
<b>You cannot possibly catch the movement of
flowing water, fluctuating speed at will.</b>

10:23.890 --> 10:26.520
<b><i>A practical sword dance
that combines movements of kenpo</i></b>

10:26.520 --> 10:28.140
<b><i>with techniques of the kodachi...</i></b>

10:28.560 --> 10:31.610
<b><i>this is how Aoshi Shinomori
truly fights!</i></b>

10:32.610 --> 10:33.440
<b>Die.</b>

10:38.400 --> 10:39.240
<b>Kenshin!</b>

10:42.070 --> 10:43.490
<b>Kaiten Kenbu...</b>

10:44.450 --> 10:48.210
<b>this technique has disposed of every
insurgent who snuck into Edo Castle.</b>

10:48.830 --> 10:49.670
<b>Ken...</b>

10:51.750 --> 10:52.590
<b>...shin.</b>

10:53.380 --> 10:54.800
<b>This is the end, boy.</b>

10:55.420 --> 10:57.260
<b>Himura Battosai is dead.</b>

10:58.920 --> 11:00.380
<b>Shut up!</b>

11:00.380 --> 11:02.340
<b>I'll take you on now!</b>

11:02.720 --> 11:06.470
<b>Even if it kills me,
I'll make sure to take you down!</b>

11:07.890 --> 11:09.190
<b>That's good spirit.</b>

11:10.140 --> 11:12.940
<b>It feels a bit shameful
to kill you here.</b>

11:14.650 --> 11:19.990
<b>Yahiko is Kamiya Kasshin-ryu's
precious successor, that he is.</b>

11:20.490 --> 11:23.070
<b>I won't let him die in a place like this.</b>

11:23.620 --> 11:28.250
<b>Besides, I can't allow myself
to die in a place like this, either!</b>

11:29.040 --> 11:29.910
<b>Kenshin!</b>

11:30.710 --> 11:32.370
<b>Are you immortal?</b>

11:32.670 --> 11:33.830
<b>Hardly.</b>

11:37.090 --> 11:38.590
<b>Kaiten Kenbu, eh?</b>

11:39.010 --> 11:42.050
<b>I didn't think it would slice apart
my metal sheath like it was a log.</b>

11:42.720 --> 11:43.970
<b>I see.</b>

11:43.970 --> 11:46.850
<b>You halved its effects with your sheath
in the spur of the moment.</b>

11:47.850 --> 11:49.600
<b>You are quite the man.</b>

11:49.600 --> 11:52.560
<b>I can see why they call you
the strongest ever.</b>

11:53.060 --> 11:56.230
<b>No, I will acknowledge myself as such.</b>

11:57.440 --> 12:02.320
<b>And this makes me want the title
of strongest within our ranks once again!</b>

12:02.740 --> 12:03.950
<b>Be careful, Kenshin!</b>

12:04.320 --> 12:05.740
<b>There's a Kaiten Kenbu coming!</b>

12:05.990 --> 12:10.040
<b>I told you. This movement of flowing water
is something you cannot capture.</b>

12:10.200 --> 12:13.170
<b>Furthermore, you are wounded all over,
and your movement is slowed...</b>

12:13.870 --> 12:16.250
<b>This is the end, Himura Battosai!</b>

12:32.640 --> 12:33.810
<b>Kenshin!</b>

12:35.940 --> 12:38.820
<b>Hiten Mitsurugi-ryu, Ryuukosen.</b>

12:39.690 --> 12:43.740
<b>This is the only unarmed technique
in Hiten Mitsurugi-ryu, that it is.</b>

12:44.530 --> 12:48.580
<b>Indeed, I cannot grasp
your movements similar to flowing water.</b>

12:49.200 --> 12:53.160
<b>However, if it's the moment where you
switch to attacking with Kaiten Kenbu,</b>

12:53.160 --> 12:54.710
<b>I can counter it, though barely!</b>

12:55.460 --> 12:58.670
<b>Aoshi, if you want
the title of strongest that badly,</b>

12:58.670 --> 13:00.420
<b>I can give it to you as much as you want.</b>

13:00.710 --> 13:04.050
<b>Such a title is annoying at best for me.</b>

13:04.430 --> 13:05.680
<b>For my current self,</b>

13:05.680 --> 13:08.140
<b>those that await my aid
and those that wait for my return</b>

13:08.140 --> 13:11.600
<b>are tens of thousands of times
more important, that they are!</b>

13:19.980 --> 13:22.990
<b>RUROUNI KENSHIN</b>

13:27.740 --> 13:30.740
<b><i>Lose? Me?</i></b>

13:30.990 --> 13:33.040
<b>Don't overdo it. Pull back!</b>

13:33.040 --> 13:35.290
<b>After two blows to the throat,
not even you—</b>

13:35.410 --> 13:37.000
<b>Not done yet!</b>

13:38.710 --> 13:40.130
<b>Kenshin!</b>

13:40.130 --> 13:42.210
<b>I'm all right... that I am.</b>

13:42.960 --> 13:44.340
<b>More than me, Aoshi...</b>

13:45.130 --> 13:47.720
<b>Is he... dead?</b>

13:47.720 --> 13:50.510
<b>No, he is just unconscious, that he is.</b>

13:50.720 --> 13:54.020
<b>After I hurt his throat
with two powerful blows,</b>

13:54.020 --> 13:58.230
<b>he unleashed an attack
that required a deep breath.</b>

13:58.730 --> 14:02.320
<b>It's only natural that he suffered
great pain and had difficulty breathing.</b>

14:03.440 --> 14:06.900
<b>In the end, the competitiveness
that never backed down...</b>

14:07.320 --> 14:10.280
<b>brought his own defeat, that it did.</b>

14:14.620 --> 14:18.500
<b>Your soulful words
when I fell to Kaiten Kenbu</b>

14:18.500 --> 14:20.210
<b>were really reassuring, that they were.</b>

14:23.380 --> 14:24.800
<b>All right!</b>

14:24.800 --> 14:28.180
<b>All we gotta do now
is take Kanryu down and rescue Megumi!</b>

14:30.010 --> 14:32.390
<b>That's quite the recuperative power.</b>

14:33.180 --> 14:35.350
<b>I fell unconscious?</b>

14:35.600 --> 14:38.230
<b>Well, for about 10 seconds, that you were.</b>

14:38.730 --> 14:41.020
<b>Why won't you deliver the final blow?</b>

14:41.020 --> 14:42.980
<b>I am currently a rurouni.</b>

14:42.980 --> 14:44.780
<b>I am not a hitokiri, that I am not.</b>

14:44.780 --> 14:47.570
<b>However, even without a final blow,</b>

14:47.570 --> 14:52.030
<b>someone of your caliber
should know who was victorious.</b>

14:53.950 --> 14:56.250
<b>Aoshi, answer one question.</b>

14:56.750 --> 14:58.830
<b>Though from the shadows,</b>

14:58.830 --> 15:02.210
<b>you took on the important role
of Oniwaban Group leader...</b>

15:02.630 --> 15:05.050
<b>there should have been
more than just one or two offers</b>

15:05.050 --> 15:06.880
<b>for officer positions
after the revolution.</b>

15:08.050 --> 15:11.220
<b>If you wanted a place to test your skills,</b>

15:11.220 --> 15:13.760
<b>surely there were other places
to choose from.</b>

15:15.220 --> 15:17.890
<b>There were plenty of offers
for officer positions.</b>

15:18.560 --> 15:20.770
<b>From intelligence in the Ground Troops</b>

15:20.770 --> 15:23.560
<b>to bodyguards of prolific politicians,
the entire spectrum.</b>

15:24.520 --> 15:27.150
<b>But they were all for me.</b>

15:28.400 --> 15:32.620
<b>Those that excel at one unusual power,
like Hyottoko and Beshimi,</b>

15:32.620 --> 15:38.750
<b>betrayers like Shikijo, and Han'nya's case
is obvious once you see his true face.</b>

15:39.330 --> 15:43.880
<b>Not one offer for officer positions
came in for others in the Oniwaban Group.</b>

15:45.750 --> 15:49.220
<b>As the leader,
how can I serve as an officer</b>

15:49.220 --> 15:51.130
<b>after abandoning all my subordinates?</b>

15:52.050 --> 15:56.350
<b>I don't want to perform a betrayal
as ugly as that of Yoshinobu Tokugawa.</b>

15:57.310 --> 15:58.390
<b>Yoshinobu was—</b>

15:58.390 --> 15:59.640
<b>I know that.</b>

16:00.810 --> 16:03.940
<b>Yoshinobu's absolute compliance,
that was a powerful political decision</b>

16:03.940 --> 16:07.320
<b>in order to not lessen
our power as a nation.</b>

16:07.690 --> 16:11.030
<b>But even then, I want none of it.</b>

16:14.910 --> 16:17.870
<b>It's been 10 years
since I've been herding the Oniwaban Group</b>

16:17.870 --> 16:20.500
<b>after being tossed out into Tokyo,
the new capital in Meiji.</b>

16:20.960 --> 16:23.620
<b>I have seen off
those that found new lives.</b>

16:24.120 --> 16:25.960
<b>I only have four subordinates left.</b>

16:27.500 --> 16:32.880
<b>Four miserable souls that only know
of battle and can do nothing but fight.</b>

16:34.050 --> 16:35.340
<b>Then at the least,</b>

16:35.340 --> 16:39.520
<b>I could add the brilliant flower
of "strongest" to the Oniwaban Group</b>

16:39.890 --> 16:41.810
<b>and turn it into their pride.</b>

16:44.350 --> 16:45.520
<b>Give me the final blow.</b>

16:46.020 --> 16:49.780
<b>If you don't,
I will come after you countless times.</b>

16:54.150 --> 16:57.700
<b>How pitiful you are, Aoshi Shinomori!</b>

16:59.240 --> 17:02.410
<b>I came out,
as I just couldn't wait anymore!</b>

17:02.620 --> 17:03.830
<b>Kanryu.</b>

17:03.830 --> 17:06.420
<b>That saves us the effort
of searching for you, that it does.</b>

17:06.670 --> 17:09.130
<b>That's quite the confidence.</b>

17:09.130 --> 17:10.130
<b>However...</b>

17:10.130 --> 17:14.170
<b>can you keep that confidence
even after seeing this?</b>

17:15.090 --> 17:15.930
<b>That is—</b>

17:15.930 --> 17:16.890
<b>It can't be...</b>

17:17.930 --> 17:18.850
<b>a Gatling gun?</b>

17:19.600 --> 17:20.760
<b>Indeed!</b>

17:20.760 --> 17:24.520
<b>Developed in 1861 by Gatling,
an American doctor,</b>

17:24.520 --> 17:26.730
<b>the ultimate weapon
that brought the Northern army</b>

17:26.730 --> 17:29.110
<b>the victory in the Civil War!</b>

17:29.610 --> 17:32.150
<b>In Japan,
the Echigo-Nagaoka Domain purchased it.</b>

17:32.150 --> 17:35.490
<b>In the Boshin War, the Third War,
and the Battle of Hokuetsu,</b>

17:35.490 --> 17:38.200
<b>this became a great threat
in the Imperial Army!</b>

17:38.530 --> 17:42.540
<b>A destructive force that can move history,
a great ability that creates a generation.</b>

17:42.540 --> 17:44.870
<b>Let's take our time to try this out!</b>

17:50.540 --> 17:52.170
<b>Wh-What was that just now?</b>

17:53.840 --> 17:55.130
<b>Ken-san...</b>

17:56.010 --> 17:57.470
<b>That was loud.</b>

17:57.470 --> 17:58.800
<b>What the hell was that?</b>

17:59.640 --> 18:02.430
<b>There seems to be some anomaly upstairs.</b>

18:02.430 --> 18:03.640
<b>Han'nya!</b>

18:03.640 --> 18:05.390
<b>Don't be so alarmed.</b>

18:06.140 --> 18:09.690
<b>Both Shikijo and I
had fair fights and lost.</b>

18:09.690 --> 18:14.400
<b>I have no intent on being the victor now
by attacking someone off their guard.</b>

18:14.820 --> 18:17.860
<b>Anyway, I am worried about Lord Aoshi.</b>

18:18.410 --> 18:21.280
<b>I will head up with Shikijo,
but what will you do?</b>

18:21.490 --> 18:24.330
<b>You know, you're a pretty good guy.</b>

18:25.000 --> 18:27.080
<b>I only hear that as sarcasm.</b>

18:28.580 --> 18:29.880
<b>No doubt.</b>

18:30.210 --> 18:31.790
<b>Wake up, Shikijo.</b>

18:35.260 --> 18:37.300
<b>Oh, it's you, Han'nya.</b>

18:37.300 --> 18:40.550
<b>Your face right when I wake up
really gets me going.</b>

18:40.550 --> 18:43.060
<b>Sheesh. Each and every one of you...</b>

18:44.270 --> 18:45.640
<b>Hey, shrimp.</b>

18:45.640 --> 18:47.020
<b>What is it, fatso?</b>

18:47.480 --> 18:49.560
<b>Did you hear that booming sound just now?</b>

18:49.810 --> 18:54.020
<b>If you heard it as well,
that means I wasn't imagining it.</b>

18:54.730 --> 18:57.820
<b>Looks like this ain't the time
to be takin' naps.</b>

19:00.410 --> 19:02.660
<b>How's that? Isn't it wonderful?</b>

19:03.450 --> 19:07.750
<b>I can fire
an amazing 200 bullets in one minute!</b>

19:07.750 --> 19:12.170
<b>That guy is not hitting us on purpose,
because he wants to torture us to death!</b>

19:12.170 --> 19:14.800
<b>Gat! Gat! Gat! Gat! Gat! Gat! Gat!</b>

19:14.800 --> 19:17.420
<b>If you stay still, I'll hit you with this!</b>

19:17.550 --> 19:19.880
<b>Kanryu! Why the hell
do you have something like that?</b>

19:19.880 --> 19:22.550
<b>That's Lord Kanryu, you insolent fool!</b>

19:24.810 --> 19:25.640
<b>Aoshi!</b>

19:26.350 --> 19:27.520
<b>Really.</b>

19:27.520 --> 19:29.600
<b>But, oh, well.</b>

19:29.600 --> 19:32.440
<b>I will let you know
as part of my smoke break.</b>

19:34.570 --> 19:39.530
<b>My ultimate ambition is to become
the most profitable dealer in the world.</b>

19:40.030 --> 19:41.910
<b>And that is a dealer of death...</b>

19:42.910 --> 19:45.330
<b>an arms dealer!</b>

19:46.790 --> 19:50.960
<b>Gathering funds through the new opium and
with this Gatling gun as the main product,</b>

19:50.960 --> 19:53.580
<b>I will make an assault on my competitors!</b>

19:53.580 --> 19:57.300
<b>That is the scenario for the birth
of the great merchant, Kanryu Takeda!</b>

19:57.510 --> 19:59.420
<b>You're going to go that far?</b>

19:59.920 --> 20:02.180
<b>You will ravage human lives and souls</b>

20:02.180 --> 20:05.470
<b>in order to get your hands on money,
that you will?</b>

20:07.180 --> 20:08.850
<b>Himura Battosai.</b>

20:09.390 --> 20:14.860
<b>How many years and sacrifices did it take
for you to gain that incredible strength?</b>

20:15.360 --> 20:19.030
<b>That surely was not gained
through extraordinary effort, was it?</b>

20:19.490 --> 20:21.530
<b>But still, if you have money,</b>

20:21.530 --> 20:24.450
<b>you can easily gain power
that surpasses even that!</b>

20:24.450 --> 20:27.450
<b>In an instant!
Without paying any sacrifices!</b>

20:27.700 --> 20:30.910
<b>Money! This is truly the proof of power!</b>

20:30.910 --> 20:35.420
<b>What was that about the Oniwaban Group
or the legendary manslayer?</b>

20:35.420 --> 20:37.420
<b>The true strongest is yours truly!</b>

20:37.420 --> 20:41.090
<b>There is nothing more wonderful
in this world than money!</b>

20:41.380 --> 20:44.050
<b>And I will prove that right now!</b>

20:44.550 --> 20:46.220
<b>Die!</b>

20:46.550 --> 20:47.850
<b>What the hell is that?</b>

20:51.270 --> 20:52.100
<b>Shikijo!</b>

20:52.100 --> 20:53.560
<b>- Wha—
- Now!</b>

20:53.560 --> 20:54.690
<b>Run, Battosai!</b>

20:57.570 --> 20:59.610
<b>Which... Which one should be the target?</b>

20:59.610 --> 21:02.820
<b>Damn it, I'll start off
with the immobile Aoshi!</b>

21:02.950 --> 21:04.610
<b>I won't let you do that!</b>

21:04.610 --> 21:06.530
<b>Gat! Gat! Gat! Gat! Gat! Gat! Gat!</b>

21:10.620 --> 21:11.580
<b>Shikijo!</b>

22:45.010 --> 22:50.010
<b>NEXT EPISODE
BATTLE'S END</b>

22:46.720 --> 22:49.260
<b><i>Next episode, "Battle's End."</i></b>
